<title><![CDATA[Who would have thought a lemon could cause so much damage?? Anyw...]]></title>
<link>https://prank-arum.GIThub.io/Feeds/TikTok/susi.vidal/7628817795488288014.mp4</link>
<guid>https://tiktok.com/embed/7628817795488288014</guid>
<description>
<![CDATA[Who would have thought a lemon could cause so much damage?? Anyways… this recipe actually slaps and one of the first I followed when I started cooking :)  it’s from Priya Krishna!!  Marinade ingredients: 8 minced garlic cloves, 3tbsp lemon juice, 2tbsp minced ginger, 3tbsp olive oil, 1tbsp finely chopped cilantro, 1tbsp finely chopped mint, 1tbsp coriander, 1tsp amchur powder, 1tsp turmeric, 3/4tsp salt, 1/2tsp red chili powder  Combine marinade with 4 chicken breasts! Let rest in the fridge for 2 hrs.  Preheat large pan on med-high heat. Add 1tsp oil and chicken. Cook each side for 2 min. Cover, and reduce heat to low and cook for 10 min. Remove from heat and let sit covered for 10-15 min! Don’t look because it’ll remove steam.chicken should be fully cooked but make sure it’s 165F!  I served with a little salad and rice! Enjoy 🥳
<img src="https://p19-common-sign.tiktokcdn-us.com/tos-useast5-p-0068-tx/owVgW2AC9IArYAkTAiA5QAIfeLIGGEHkeGvjvL~tplv-tiktokx-origin.image?dr=9636&amp;x-expires=1787702400&amp;x-signature=rPH643f1yQWw7lk4ic1YjZaiz8s%3D&amp;t=4d5b0474&amp;ps=13740610&amp;shp=81f88b70&amp;shcp=43f4a2f9&amp;idc=useast8" /><br><a href="https://tiktok.com/@susi.vidal/video/7628817795488288014">FULL POST</a> | <a href="https://tiktok.com/embed/7628817795488288014">EMBED</a> | <a href="https://ezgif.com/rotate-video?url=https://prank-arum.GIThub.io/Feeds/TikTok/susi.vidal/7628817795488288014.mp4">REVERSED</a><br>]]>
